// Title: Scheduled Cron Task/Job - Linux
// Sigma ID: 6b14bac8-3e3a-4324-8109-42f0546a347f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Alejandro Ortuno, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-06 | Modified: 2022-11-27
// ATT&CK: execution, persistence, privilege-escalation, T1053.003
// Description: Detects abuse of the cron utility to perform task scheduling for initial or recurring execution
//   of malicious code. Detection will focus on crontab jobs uploaded from the tmp folder.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1053.003/T1053.003.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_schedule_task_job_cron.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "crontab" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/tmp/"
